			<div class="content" id="post-content-2152588">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Grimdark isn't the only way to go, people.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is this still repeated like it's a 'thing', like everyone insists upon it? Probably the <em>majority</em> of articles from the past couple years have made no attempt at all at being grimdark. There are anime catgirls, flying fart-cows <em>and</em> -monkeys, and cockgoblins around here now, and three of those four are mainlist articles. Why even say that?</p>
<p>On-topic: I rarely appreciate the re-packaging of old mythological figures, so I'm biased right from the main idea of this. Jack trying to get his old feelgoodz back is alright, and if it was done&#8230;tastefully?&#8230;enough, I could dig it, but to me this seems like the addition of a pile of cliches. The logs seem to include every character from every party scene from every comedy movie and D.A.R.E. spot made. On the plus side, I choose to believe that I saw the Night at the Roxbury guys in there, and that's slightly cool.</p>

