			<div class="content" id="post-content-2152479">
									

<p><em>Most of this was addressed in the chat when you had the conversation with me about it.</em> As I said then and I will say now, you are perfectly respected to your sense of taste and if we disagree stylistically that's totally OK.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The anomaly is lackluster - if the creature is supposedly magical in nature, given that it used to do magic stuff before becoming the scravecrow, one would have said a rave with such anomaly would be much more crazier</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It says in the last interview that scravecrow wants no trouble, no hurt, no violence. Scravecrow just wants to relive some kind of feeling from his past. He has absolutely no reason to make it &quot;much more crazier&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Researchers and MFTs, which we should remember are specially trained to deal with the SCPs they are assigned to</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The first log was <em>first contact</em>, as stated in the logs themselves. The second log was maybe 4th contact, where they were much better for it.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>socially inept research</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I don't actually understand what this means. The researcher wasn't really socially inept for having a few uhs, is she? Jesus, that makes me super socially inept.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Then there's the whole ditz teenager stereotype on the hands of the girl.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>As I said before,this was based on things I hear coming out of people's mouths in raves. I've edited it since to tone it down.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There's also the fact that they are called interviews, but interviews are not that from what I know, those are an event's sound recordings, not a premeditated interview.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You can have non-premeditated interviews. I didn't have a better word, but if you find one I would love to know.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This line treats something that should be assumed of a rave as if it was worthy of mention.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No, the line is a basic demographics of the population of people that attend the party. O_o</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This line implies that people drink more alcohol and drugs than normal in a rave, but how much is not pointed out anywhere.</p>
