			<div class="content" id="post-content-2152493">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Scravecrow just wants to relive some kind of feeling from his past. He has absolutely no reason to make it &quot;much more crazier&quot;.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>&quot;Well, I could tell you plenty about him, but you probably won't believe me. He used to be called Jack, y'know, of the lantern variety. Used to do a lot of work, changing the color of the leaves and making things foggy on dark nights. He was a bit of seasonal worker if y'know what I'm saying.&quot;</p>
<p>See this line. Jack, judging by what he did before, could easily use his abilities to enhance the party without hurting anybody. It doesn't need to be violent.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The first log was first contact, as stated in the logs themselves. The second log was maybe 4th contact, where they were much better for it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Unless there researcher happens to be the very first authority to come across the the SCP, being unprepared is not a wise thing to do, I mean, we are talking about a party that literally materializes and dematerializes, there's got to be rumours or foundation-contact worthy worries on part of the police and other authorities.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I don't actually understand what this means. The researcher wasn't really socially inept for having a few uhs, is she? Jesus, that makes me super socially inept.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Socially inept enough to potentially botch the mission, as given that the approach towards contact was non-violent. You gotta know how to talk your way to the DJ. Not to mention that like the girl said she could just google his name if acquiring second hand info on him was the mission.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As I said before,this was based on things I hear coming out of people's mouths in raves. I've edited it since to tone it down.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It's a rather common stereotype of the clubbing girl. Yes, there's people that talks like this, but they are a minority.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You can have non-premeditated interviews. I didn't have a better word, but if you find one I would love to know.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The best thing I can think of is &quot;audio extract&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No, the line is a basic demographics of the population of people that attend the party. O_o</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And those demographics do not go beyond what is expected of raves (regardless of how we feel at the fact that 13 years old do go to raves). So it could be simplified in order to read better.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This isn't necessary because the only purpose was an implication, that's it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Well, if you make a statement, you sort of have to write down it's cause or hypothesized cause too. I mean, if I'm an O5 and someone gives me a report saying &quot;X thing happens more than normal&quot;, I'd be interested in knowing why. Case in context could be thematic (basically showering you with get high messages or facilitating access to drugs) or anomalous.</p>

